---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Wordmark from '../components/Wordmark.astro';
import { formatDate } from '../data/format-date';

const lastUpdated = '2026-09-05';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — Common Mechanics"
  description="How Common Mechanics Ltd handles personal data. No cookies, no analytics, no tracking — only what is needed to serve the page, and the email you choose to send us."
>
  <main class="privacy">
    <header class="section privacy-header" data-rule="bottom">
      <Wordmark href="/" class="privacy-back-top" />
      <h1 class="privacy-title">Privacy notice</h1>
      <p class="privacy-lede">
        This site sets no cookies, runs no analytics and asks you for nothing. Here is
        exactly what does happen to personal data, and what you can do about it.
      </p>
      <p class="privacy-updated">
        Last updated <time datetime={lastUpdated}>{formatDate(lastUpdated)}</time>
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="section privacy-body" data-rule="bottom" aria-labelledby="who-we-are">
      <h2 id="who-we-are">Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        Common Mechanics Ltd is the data controller for everything described on this page.
        We are registered in England and Wales, company number 17385700, with a registered
        office at 71–75 Shelton Street, London, WC2H 9JQ.
      </p>
      <p>
        For anything to do with privacy or your data, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@commonmechanics.io">privacy@commonmechanics.io</a>.
      </p>
      <!-- TODO: add ICO registration number once confirmed -->

      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        This is a handful of static pages. No cookies. No analytics. No tag manager, no
        tracking pixels, no third-party embeds, no forms, no accounts, no newsletter.
      </p>

      <h2>What we process, why, and on what basis</h2>

      <h3>Visiting this site</h3>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider receives your IP address, the page you asked for and standard
        request headers such as your browser and language. No website can serve or protect a
        connection without them, and ours is no exception. We keep no logs of our own, so we
        hold no per-visitor record we could look you up in. The provider processes this data
        at its edge on our behalf to route and deliver the page and to defend the site
        against attack and abuse, and retains it under its own retention schedule. Which
        company that is, and where it processes the data, is recorded in the sub-processor
        list on our <a href="/data-processing">data processing page</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Purpose.</strong> Delivering this website and keeping it available and secure.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Lawful basis.</strong> Legitimate interests, Article 6(1)(f) — running a site
        people can reach and defending it from attack.
      </p>

      <h3>Emailing us</h3>
      <p>
        If you write to <a href="mailto:privacy@commonmechanics.io">privacy@commonmechanics.io</a>
        or to any of the team addresses published on this site, we process your email address,
        your name if you give it, anything else you put in the message or its attachments, and
        our reply.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Purpose.</strong> Receiving and responding to email queries.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Lawful basis.</strong> Performance of a contract or steps taken at your
        request before entering one, Article 6(1)(b), where you are asking about working with
        us. Otherwise legitimate interests, Article 6(1)(f) — replying to people who get in
        touch. If you send us a request about your own data, we handle it under our legal
        obligation, Article 6(1)(c).
      </p>
      <p>
        Please do not send us special-category data — health, beliefs, anything of that kind.
        We have no reason to need it and would rather not hold it.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and similar technology</h2>
      <p>
        None at all. No cookies, no local storage, no fingerprinting, nothing stored on or
        read from your device beyond what is strictly needed to deliver the page you asked
        for. Because of that, regulation 6 of PECR does not require your consent, which is
        why there is no cookie banner in your way. Our typefaces are served from this site
        rather than from a third-party font CDN, so loading a page does not tell anyone else
        that you were here.
      </p>

      <h2>Links out</h2>
      <p>
        The portfolio and team sections link to other websites, including LinkedIn and our
        clients' own sites. Nothing from those sites is embedded here, so they learn nothing
        about you until you click. Once you do, you are on their infrastructure under their
        privacy policy, not ours.
      </p>

      <h2>Who else sees your data</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Our hosting provider</strong> — hosting and content delivery for this site,
          acting as our processor.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Our email provider</strong> — stores and delivers the mail we send and
          receive, acting as our processor.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Both are named — legal entity, function and processing locations — in the versioned
        sub-processor list on our <a href="/data-processing">data processing page</a>. That
        list is where we keep the record current, so a change of supplier shows up there
        rather than going unnoticed here.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is the whole list. We do not sell personal data, share it with advertisers or
        data brokers, or use it to train anything. The only other circumstance in which we
        would disclose it is where the law requires us to — a court order or a regulator's
        lawful request.
      </p>

      <h2>Where your data goes</h2>
      <p>
        Our hosting provider serves this site from a global network, so your request is
        usually handled by whichever data centre is nearest you, which may be outside the UK.
        It acts as our processor, and its data protection terms rely on standard contractual
        clauses together with the UK International Data Transfer Addendum — the safeguard UK
        GDPR provides for transfers of this kind. Our email provider may process mail outside
        the UK under the same sort of safeguard. Beyond that, we make no international
        transfers of personal data in connection with this site.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep things</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Request data.</strong> We hold none. Our hosting provider holds connection
          and security logs briefly under its own retention schedule; we cannot retrieve them
          and do not keep a copy.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Email.</strong> We do not run a deletion clock against your messages. We
          keep correspondence while it is live, and afterwards for as long as we could still
          need it to answer a question about the work — a contractual, tax, insurance or
          legal one — after which it goes. Ask us and we will tell you what we still hold
          from a particular exchange.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK GDPR you can ask us to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>give you a copy of the personal data we hold about you, and tell you what we do with it (access);</li>
        <li>correct anything that is wrong or incomplete (rectification);</li>
        <li>delete it (erasure);</li>
        <li>pause what we are doing with it while a question about it is resolved (restriction);</li>
        <li>hand it to you, or to someone else, in a portable machine-readable format, where we hold it by consent or under a contract and process it by automated means (portability);</li>
        <li>stop processing it where we rely on legitimate interests (objection).</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not currently rely on consent for anything on this site, so there is nothing to
        withdraw. If that ever changes, you will be able to withdraw consent at any time and
        as easily as you gave it, and doing so will not affect anything done beforehand.
        There is no automated decision-making or profiling here, and no direct marketing.
      </p>
      <p>
        To use any of these rights, email
        <a href="mailto:privacy@commonmechanics.io">privacy@commonmechanics.io</a>. We will
        reply within one month. We may need to be reasonably sure of
        who you are before we hand over data — replying from the address we already
        correspond with is normally enough. Some of these rights have limits, and if we
        cannot do what you have asked we will tell you plainly why.
      </p>

      <h2>Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        Come to us first if you can, at
        <a href="mailto:privacy@commonmechanics.io">privacy@commonmechanics.io</a> — it is
        usually the fastest way to get something fixed. You are not obliged to, and you can
        complain to the UK regulator, the Information Commissioner's Office, at any time.
      </p>
      <ul class="privacy-contact">
        <li>
          <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener noreferrer">ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint</a>
        </li>
        <li>Helpline <a href="tel:+443031231113">0303 123 1113</a></li>
        <li>Information Commissioner's Office, Wycliffe House, Water Lane, Wilmslow, Cheshire, SK9 5AF</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
      <p>
        If we ever add something to this site that processes personal data — a contact form,
        analytics, an embed — we will update this page before it goes live and change the
        date at the top.
      </p>
    </section>

    <nav class="section privacy-back" aria-label="Back to the home page">
      <a href="/">Back to the home page</a>
    </nav>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ─── Header band ──────────────────────────────── */
  .privacy-header {
    padding-top: var(--space-16);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-12);
  }

  .privacy-back-top {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .privacy-title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(var(--font-size-xl), 6vw, var(--font-size-2xl));
    font-weight: 300;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    line-height: 1.15;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }

  .privacy-lede {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
  }

  .privacy-updated {
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
  }

  /* ─── Body band ────────────────────────────────── */
  .privacy-body {
    /* Long addresses and URLs must not push the page sideways at 320px */
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .privacy-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.3;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-accent-line);
    padding-top: var(--space-6);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  /* First heading sits flush with the top of the band */
  .privacy-body h2:first-child {
    border-top: 0;
    padding-top: 0;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .privacy-body h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
  }

  .privacy-body p,
  .privacy-body li {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-base);
    line-height: 1.7;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .privacy-body p + p {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .privacy-body strong {
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .privacy-body ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .privacy-body li {
    position: relative;
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
  }

  .privacy-body li + li {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  /* Technical-drawing dash instead of a bullet */
  .privacy-body li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.75em;
    width: var(--space-3);
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--color-rule);
  }

  .privacy-contact {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  .privacy-contact li {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
  }

  /* ─── Back band ────────────────────────────────── */
  .privacy-back {
    padding-top: var(--space-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-24);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-wide);
  }

  /* ─── Focus ────────────────────────────────────── */
  a:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--color-fg);
    outline-offset: 3px;
    border-radius: 1px;
  }
</style>
